<%/* An agent's message: its words, and the visuals it drew, in the order it
     wrote them (D-v3x). The server splits the message on its top-level fences
     and hands each piece over ready to print:
       - text: the words between, rendered as markdown (html);
       - flow, map: a visual Prelude read and checked, drawn with the design
         system's flow or map (_visual-flow, _visual-map);
       - drawing: a visual the agent is still writing (only while it streams),
         a placeholder until its block is complete (_visual-drawing);
       - unread: a block tagged as a visual that Prelude couldn't read, shown
         as the agent wrote it, with why (_visual-unread).
     A message with no visuals is one text piece. `it` has pieces, and the
     live entry's id while it streams, which makes this its region.

     A part on a visual opens its page in the drawer, over the conversation,
     so the session stays where it was (the person, 2026-10-23). */%>
<div class="stack gap-3 message"<% if (it.id) { %> id="<%= it.id %>-text" ko-region<% } %>>
<% for (const piece of it.pieces ?? []) { %>
<% if (piece.kind === 'text') { %>
  <div class="prose"><%~ piece.html %></div>
<% } else if (piece.kind === 'flow') { %>
  <%~ include('./_visual-flow', { ...piece.flow, target: 'drawer?' }) %>
<% } else if (piece.kind === 'map') { %>
  <%~ include('./_visual-map', { ...piece.map, target: 'drawer?' }) %>
<% } else if (piece.kind === 'drawing') { %>
  <%~ include('./_visual-drawing', piece) %>
<% } else { %>
  <%~ include('./_visual-unread', piece) %>
<% } %>
<% } %>
</div>
